      },
      "findings": [
        {
          "source_quote": "ὡς εἰς ἀέναον ἐβάπτισεν ὕδωρ",
          "english_quote": "baptized me in water as ever-flowing water",
          "issue": "The draft retains the relevant vocabulary, but its repeated “water” obscures the construction: ὡς qualifies the phrase εἰς ἀέναον … ὕδωρ. The note says only that the qualification is preserved; it does not explain whether ὡς is taken comparatively or as characterizing the water used.",
          "suggested_revision": "Compare the more source-transparent proposal “baptized me as into ever-flowing water.” Explain the chosen force of ὡς in a note, preserving the alternative understanding that the springs provided water treated as continuously flowing. Do not add a claim that the water was only apparently flowing. Any replacement requires fresh review.",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ἡμέρας? τεσσαράκοντα",
          "english_quote": "for forty days",
          "issue": "The draft does not disclose the question mark printed after ἡμέρας. It need not become an English question, and it does not make the surviving phrase untranslatable, but silently dropping this unusual editorial feature leaves the source disclosure incomplete.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a nonblocking source_issues entry quoting “ἡμέρας? τεσσαράκοντα,” recording the supplied question mark without calling it an OCR error or claiming its editorial purpose has been established. Retain “for forty days.” The three-dot lacuna elsewhere in the section is already explicitly preserved without restoration.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
